  "quality_flags": [
    {
      "flag_type": "unresolved_inconsistency",
      "slot": "postconditions",
      "detail": "[mainflow_postconditions_reachability] Main Flow step 5 states that accepting via the Credit Card Option immediately generates the order and ships the item, while the PayPal/Amazon path generates the order and places it in Hold until payment. Postcondition 4, however, requires that after transfer/order generation the system displays the Returning Winners Payments Page with options to choose shipping speed and checkout method. An already shipped or held order cannot still require shipping-speed and checkout-method selection, so the main flow does not reasonably lead to this postcondition.",
      "evidence_refs": []
    },
    {
      "flag_type": "unresolved_inconsistency",
      "slot": "main_flow",
      "detail": "[goal_mainflow_alignment] The goal is anchored on transferring cancelled winning orders to second-place finishers at their last bid price, but main_flow only describes verification, emailing the second-place finisher, option selection, and generating a new order. It never states that the winning order is cancelled or that the generated order is the transfer of the cancelled order. This leaves the main flow inconsistent with the goal's start/success boundary.",
      "evidence_refs": []
    }
  ],
